WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:17.090
stared at the spot in the trees where her pod should be.

2
00:00:17.110 --> 00:00:19.071
"It can't be gone!"

3
00:00:19.411 --> 00:00:19.831
she thought.

4
00:00:19.851 --> 00:00:21.652
"It has to be here somewhere."

5
00:00:21.672 --> 00:00:23.992
"Alpha!" Ally cried.

6
00:00:24.013 --> 00:00:25.513
"Where are you?"

7
00:00:26.273 --> 00:00:27.194
There was no answer.

8
00:00:29.275 --> 00:00:32.496
Ally spent the next thirty minutes looking high and low for the pod.

9
00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:41.446
She'd been trying not to think the worst, but she couldn't hold the thought off any longer.

10
00:00:41.466 --> 00:00:45.909
"Dr. Lloyd's machine finally worked," she thought.

11
00:00:45.929 --> 00:00:47.570
"He found my pod.

12
00:00:49.031 --> 00:00:52.753
And if he can find my pod, it won't be long before he finds me!"

13
00:01:00.497 --> 00:01:03.459
Ally was close to tears as she sat down on a park bench.

14
00:01:04.919 --> 00:01:07.981
With her pod gone, there was no hope she'd ever get back home.

15
00:01:10.063 --> 00:01:13.025
But even worse, she'd lost a friend—Alpha.

16
00:01:13.946 --> 00:01:16.347
Ally replayed their last morning together in her mind.

17
00:01:18.429 --> 00:01:22.592
That's when she realized what had happened: she'd forgotten to camouflage the pod!

18
00:01:23.592 --> 00:01:24.653
"Oh no!"

19
00:01:26.735 --> 00:01:28.896
she moaned, burying her head in her hands.

20
00:01:28.916 --> 00:01:31.538
"My parents were right about me.

21
00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:34.200
I am totally irresponsible!"

22
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:38.882
"Ally?" Mateo rode up on his bicycle.

23
00:01:38.902 --> 00:01:39.943
"What's wrong?"

24
00:01:41.544 --> 00:01:44.146
"It's all my fault, Mateo!"

25
00:01:44.666 --> 00:01:45.266
Ally moaned.

26
00:01:45.286 --> 00:01:47.088
"What's your fault?"

27
00:01:47.548 --> 00:01:48.649
Ally heard a girl say.

28
00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:51.571
It was Bethany's voice, but Ally didn't see her.

29
00:01:52.952 --> 00:01:56.034
Mateo held up his phone—Bethany was on speakerphone.

30
00:01:57.675 --> 00:02:00.837
Ally shook her head, to show Mateo she couldn't talk about it with Bethany.

31
00:02:02.798 --> 00:02:05.040
"Not fault," Mateo said quickly.

32
00:02:05.584 --> 00:02:07.185
"Ally told me to halt.

33
00:02:07.885 --> 00:02:08.685
She was joking.

34
00:02:09.286 --> 00:02:10.546
I'll, uh, call you later."

35
00:02:10.566 --> 00:02:12.567
"Oh, okay.

36
00:02:12.827 --> 00:02:14.848
I—," Bethany began as Mateo hung up.

37
00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.929
"What happened, Ally?"

38
00:02:17.289 --> 00:02:17.749
he asked.

39
00:02:17.769 --> 00:02:20.570
"You look like you've lost your best friend."

40
00:02:21.991 --> 00:02:22.711
"I did."

41
00:02:24.092 --> 00:02:24.672
Ally sighed.

42
00:02:24.692 --> 00:02:30.895
"Alpha warned me not to forget to camouflage the pod when we left, but I was so busy

43
00:02:30.975 --> 00:02:33.896
trying to make you laugh, I totally forgot!"

44
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.121
"I don't understand.

45
00:02:36.681 --> 00:02:37.862
What happened to Alpha?"

46
00:02:38.722 --> 00:02:39.803
"It's not just Alpha!"

47
00:02:40.143 --> 00:02:40.663
Ally said.

48
00:02:40.683 --> 00:02:42.904
"It's the entire pod.

49
00:02:43.545 --> 00:02:46.686
I forgot to camouflage it after we left, and Dr.

50
00:02:46.746 --> 00:02:48.207
Lloyd must have found it!

51
00:02:48.847 --> 00:02:50.228
What am I going to do?

52
00:02:50.989 --> 00:02:55.891
How am I going to ever get back home, and where am I going to sleep until then?"

53
00:02:55.911 --> 00:02:58.032
"Whoa, whoa."

54
00:02:58.473 --> 00:03:00.534
Mateo gestured for Ally to slow down.

55
00:03:00.554 --> 00:03:02.815
"One problem at a time.

56
00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:04.836
Maybe someone moved the pod.

57
00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:06.941
Let's not jump to conclusions."

58
00:03:09.243 --> 00:03:11.264
"I'm not jumping anywhere."

59
00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:13.005
Ally sniffled.

60
00:03:13.025 --> 00:03:16.768
"I meant, we won't know what happened until we look.

61
00:03:17.748 --> 00:03:18.149
Come on.

62
00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:19.509
Let's search some more."

63
00:03:22.231 --> 00:03:26.234
Ally and Mateo walked through the entire park, but the pod was nowhere to be found.

64
00:03:34.219 --> 00:03:35.240
Lloyd has it."

65
00:03:35.904 --> 00:03:36.525
Ally sighed.

66
00:03:37.285 --> 00:03:40.127
"He said he was certain he'd lured a ship to Earth.

67
00:03:40.607 --> 00:03:45.550
He probably took it to the UFO museum, but I can't risk going there to look for it."

68
00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:48.072
"Don't worry," Mateo said.

69
00:03:48.092 --> 00:03:50.173
"I'll go there first thing in the morning.

70
00:03:50.894 --> 00:03:52.735
We'll find your pod and Alpha.

71
00:03:53.335 --> 00:03:53.976
I promise.

72
00:03:54.636 --> 00:03:56.918
And until then you'll stay with Papi and me."

73
00:03:56.938 --> 00:04:00.060
"That's so nice of you."

74
00:04:05.544 --> 00:04:06.525
Ally blew her nose.

75
00:04:11.149 --> 00:04:13.631
what if your dad finds out I'm an Astralian?"

76
00:04:13.651 --> 00:04:20.316
"You'll just have to be careful to take off your meld medallion only at night, after Papi has

77
00:04:20.376 --> 00:04:21.037
gone to bed."

78
00:04:21.057 --> 00:04:24.980
"You don't think he'll mind having me stay?"

79
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.961
"Of course not."

80
00:04:27.722 --> 00:04:28.943
Mateo pulled out his phone.

81
00:04:28.963 --> 00:04:31.025
"Hi, Papi.

82
00:04:31.365 --> 00:04:32.105
We need a favor."

83
00:04:32.125 --> 00:04:35.008
"Whatever you need, son," Ray said.

84
00:04:36.176 --> 00:04:37.937
"Ally needs to stay with us for a while.

85
00:04:38.677 --> 00:04:41.858
You see, her place went—" "Say no more," Ray replied.

86
00:04:41.878 --> 00:04:44.498
"Ally can stay in your mom's sewing room.

87
00:04:45.138 --> 00:04:46.979
It's not being used for anything anyway."

88
00:04:46.999 --> 00:04:49.720
"Thanks, Papi!"

89
00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.800
Mateo disconnected the call.

90
00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.081
"See? We'll help you!"

91
00:04:54.621 --> 00:04:55.821
Ally managed a smile.

92
00:04:56.822 --> 00:05:00.122
"I'm very lucky to have you and Ray for friends."

93
00:05:00.142 --> 00:05:04.244
"We're lucky to have you too," Mateo said.

94
00:05:04.264 --> 00:05:05.684
"Let's go home.

95
00:05:06.168 --> 00:05:07.889
We'll find your ship and Alpha.

96
00:05:08.369 --> 00:05:09.190
I know we will."

97
00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:18.375
As the two friends walked back to Ray's house, Ally felt a mixture of emotions.

98
00:05:19.715 --> 00:05:23.377
She was really sad about losing Alpha and worried she might never get back home.

99
00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:30.341
But she tried to think of positive things, as Alpha had advised her earlier that day.

100
00:05:30.361 --> 00:05:35.124
"At least I'm learning to be a good Astralian," Ally said.

101
00:05:35.792 --> 00:05:40.873
"Funny how it took being light-years from home to understand what it means to be helpful."

102
00:05:40.893 --> 00:05:45.975
"You're the most helpful person I know," Mateo said.

103
00:05:45.995 --> 00:05:48.496
"You're even willing to help weird Barry."

104
00:05:49.056 --> 00:05:49.656
Ally laughed.

105
00:05:50.376 --> 00:05:57.558
"Hey! If I manage to teach Barry my levitation trick without making a mess of it, I might

106
00:05:57.618 --> 00:06:00.339
even win an Astralian Super Helper medal!"
